# ==============================================================================
# IO74: Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL) -> Map -> Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL) upsert (Python)
# Author: Mike Nimer <mikenimer@google.com>
#
# DAG: CloudSQL Source (parameterized SQLAlchemy SELECT) ➔ Map (mark fulfilled)
#      ➔ CloudSQL Sink (upsert, created_at preserved via updateIgnores)
# Credentials: passwordSecret values are Secret Manager SHORT IDs, resolved once at
# pipeline construction. No connection URL contains a password.
# ==============================================================================
nodes:
  - id: "source-cloudsql-1"
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 80
      y: 150
    data:
      label: Cloud SQL Orders
      type: SOURCE
      iconName: Database
      beam_transform: CloudSQL
      properties:
        cloudSqlInstance: "retail-prod-123:us-central1:orders-pg"
        dbDriver: "postgresql+pg8000"
        database: "orders"
        username: "beam_reader"
        passwordSecret: "orders-pg-reader-password"
        query: "SELECT order_id, customer_id, status, total_amount, created_at FROM orders WHERE status = :status"
        queryParams: '{"status": "PAID"}'
      system_instructions: "Implement this Cloud SQL source following the jccatrinck/dataflow-cloud-sql-python ReadFromDBFn pattern, connecting with the Cloud SQL Python Connector (google.cloud.sql.connector) and SQLAlchemy 2.x. A custom DoFn is REQUIRED here because Beam has no built-in Cloud SQL SQLAlchemy source: seed it with p | 'Seed Cloud SQL Read' >> beam.Create([{}]) followed by beam.ParDo(ReadFromDBFn(...)). Resolve passwordSecret ONCE at pipeline construction with _access_secret(project_id, 'orders-pg-reader-password') and pass only the resolved string into the DoFn constructor. Parse queryParams ('{\"status\": \"PAID\"}') with json.loads into query_params={'status': 'PAID'}. In ReadFromDBFn.setup() create Connector() and sqlalchemy.create_engine('postgresql+pg8000://', creator=lambda: connector.connect('retail-prod-123:us-central1:orders-pg', 'pg8000', user='beam_reader', password=<resolved>, db='orders')); the 'postgresql+pg8000' dialect and the 'pg8000' driver name come from dbDriver. NEVER build a connection URL that contains the password (no user:password@ form) and never log it. In teardown() call engine.dispose() and connector.close(). In process() use the SQLAlchemy 2.x API: with engine.connect() as conn: result = conn.execute(sqlalchemy.text(query), params) where params is query_params ({'status': 'PAID'}) overridden by element['db_query_params'] when present; yield dict(row._mapping) for each row. Never format values into the SQL string. requirements.txt must include cloud-sql-python-connector[pg8000], SQLAlchemy>=2.0 and google-cloud-secret-manager."
    width: 180
    height: 62
  - id: "step-map-2"
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 360
      y: 150
    data:
      label: Mark Fulfilled
      type: STEP
      iconName: Code
      beam_transform: Map
      system_instructions: "For each order dict, return a new dict with the same keys (order_id, customer_id, status, total_amount, created_at) where status is set to 'FULFILLED' and all other fields are unchanged. Implement it as a named module-level function (not a lambda) and unit-test that function with TestPipeline, beam.Create and assert_that/equal_to. Unit tests must not open database or Secret Manager connections."
    width: 180
    height: 62
  - id: "sink-cloudsql-3"
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 640
      y: 150
    data:
      label: Cloud SQL Fulfilled Orders
      type: SINK
      iconName: Database
      beam_transform: CloudSQL
      properties:
        cloudSqlInstance: "retail-prod-123:us-central1:analytics-pg"
        dbDriver: "postgresql+pg8000"
        database: "analytics"
        username: "beam_writer"
        passwordSecret: "analytics-pg-writer-password"
        table: "fulfilled_orders"
        updateIgnores: "created_at"
      system_instructions: "Implement this sink as a composite beam.PTransform named WriteIntoDB mirroring the jccatrinck/dataflow-cloud-sql-python WriteIntoDB(url, table, update_ignores) contract, taking the Cloud SQL Connector settings and SQLAlchemy 2.x API. Resolve passwordSecret ONCE at pipeline construction with _access_secret(project_id, 'analytics-pg-writer-password') and pass only the resolved string into the transform. Parse updateIgnores ('created_at') into update_ignores=('created_at',). In expand(): beam.BatchElements(min_batch_size=50, max_batch_size=500) then beam.ParDo(_UpsertBatchFn(...)). In _UpsertBatchFn.setup() create Connector() and sqlalchemy.create_engine('postgresql+pg8000://', creator=lambda: connector.connect('retail-prod-123:us-central1:analytics-pg', 'pg8000', user='beam_writer', password=<resolved>, db='analytics')) with no password in any URL, then reflect the target table with sqlalchemy.Table('fulfilled_orders', sqlalchemy.MetaData(), autoload_with=engine). In process(batch): stmt = sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql.insert(tbl).values(list(batch)); stmt = stmt.on_conflict_do_update(index_elements=[c.name for c in tbl.primary_key.columns], set_={c.name: stmt.excluded[c.name] for c in tbl.columns if not c.primary_key and c.name not in update_ignores}); execute inside with engine.begin() as conn. update_ignores = ('created_at',) so created_at keeps its original value on conflict. In teardown() dispose the engine and close the connector."
    width: 180
    height: 62
edges:
  - id: e-source-cloudsql-1-step-map-2
    source: "source-cloudsql-1"
    target: "step-map-2"
  - id: e-step-map-2-sink-cloudsql-3
    source: "step-map-2"
    target: "sink-cloudsql-3"
runtimeVariables:
  - key: JOB_ID
    value: cloudsql-orders-sync
jobConfig:
  runner: DirectRunner
  machineType: n1-standard-1
  minInstances: 1
  maxInstances: 5
  gcsStagingPath: ""
  network: ""
  subnetwork: ""
pipelineConfig:
  language: Python
  outputFolder: test/cloudsql-examples/cloudsql-orders-sync
  needsRebuild: false
